From 45eb8c9f0c7175e46ac64e9e20d4973393c191ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 07:12:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 048/102] render: text layers are image layers, laid out and
 sized the way Wallpaper Engine does
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Decoded from wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485 (GH = the headless Ghidra decompile):
- WE's text class extends its image class (its constructor GH 0x14027c1b0 calls the image's,
  GH 0x140212c50), so a text object takes effects, a parent, angles, parallax, alpha, colour,
  brightness and blend modes like an image. Text is now `Text : Image` in the model (parseText builds
  the image data; its model is a genericimage2 material on `_rt_textLayer_<id>`) and CText a CImage
  whose texture is its laid-out text. CScene creates CText before CImage.
- The property table (GH 0x14027e130) and constructor defaults: font systemfont_arial, pointsize 32,
  padding 32 32, spacing 0 0, maxwidth 500, maxrows 1; horizontalalign left 0 / center 1 / right 2,
  verticalalign bottom 0 / center 1 / top 2; flags opaquebackground 2, limitwidth 4, limitrows 8,
  limituseellipsis 0x10, blockalign 0x20; anchor none..topleft (0..9), all parsed.
- Size: FT_Set_Char_Size (0, pointsize * 64, 300 dpi), pointsize clamped to 1..256 (GH 0x1401d94c0,
  0x1401dd330): a 32 pt text is 133 px in the layer, which its scale then shrinks.
- Layout (GH 0x1401dd330, TextLayout): lines split at '\n'; glyph advance = advance >> 6 + spacing.x;
  line height = size metrics height >> 6 + spacing.y; each line aligned in the block (the widest
  line) by horizontalalign; the block spans the glyphs' ink and every line's 0..ascender, down to
  ascender - rows * line height. Also decoded and in TextLayout, wired by the next patch: the wrap at
  the last space before the glyph ending past maxwidth, maxrows with "…", blockalign justification.
- The layer's size is the block, plus the padding (clamped to 512) on each side while it has effects
  (GH 0x14027dd90; the glyphs are drawn at padding - min, GH 0x14027d250); an empty text is 2 x 2.
- Its quad sits at an offset from the origin (GH 0x14027c600): x = +-width/2 for left/right; y = the
  block's centre minus the ascender (top), (ascender - (rows-1) * line height) / 2 (center) or
  descender - (rows-1) * line height (bottom). CImage::setLocalOffset places the quad by it; it turns
  and scales with the layer about the origin.
- Fonts: the scene's (or WE's) fonts/… file; a systemfont_* name maps to the Windows family WE
  opens (arial.ttf, calibri.ttf, cambria.ttc, comic.ttf, consola.ttf, micross.ttf, segoeui.ttf,
  verdana.ttf), found through fontconfig with metric-compatible and generic families after it; an
  unreadable font falls back to systemfont_arial (WE: arial.ttf, GH 0x1401d9d70). A character the font
  lacks comes from a fontconfig font that has it. Text is UTF-8.
- When the text, its size or its colour changes, the texture is redrawn and the layer's composite and
  effect FBOs are resized in place (CFBO::resize, CImage::resizeTargets), so the passes stay built.

Not WE's: glyphs come from FreeType with the font's kern table (WE shapes with HarfBuzz); the texture
is mipmapped; the colour is drawn into the texture (genericimage2 doesn't take g_Color4 here), alpha
and brightness stay live in the pass. WPENGINE_TEXT_DEBUG logs each text's size next to the editor's.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B4 (T1/E34, T3, T4, T8, T10, G04 text, G13, G30; T2 lines)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01288H8XbjUdhpEVfhFbe7bj
